Buchberger's algorithm processes S-polynomials one at a time. F4 (Faugère 1999) batches many S-polynomial reductions into a single sparse-matrix row echelon computation, which is dramatically faster for medium and large ideals because the linear algebra dominates and can be optimized (cache-friendly sparse rows, the ℤ_p native i64 fast path). use ocas_domain::{RationalDomain, Rational};
