A Pattern describes an expression structure with wildcards. Three wildcard levels are available, triggered by the wildcard name suffix: Level Name suffix Matches WildcardLevel::Single _ (e.g. x_) Any single sub-expression WildcardLevel::Sequence __ (e.g. __x) One or more operands in an ordered list WildcardLevel::NullSequence ___ (e.g. ___x) Zero or more operands in an ordered list let arena = Arena::new();
let ctx = AtomArena::new(&arena); // Pattern: x + y_ where y_ matches any single sub-expression
let x = ctx.var("x");
let pat = Pattern::Add(vec![ Pattern::Literal(x), Pattern::Wildcard(Symbol::new("y_"), WildcardLevel::Single),
]); // Match: x + 5 → binds y_ to 5
let e = parse(&ctx, "x + 5").unwrap();
let bindings = match_pattern(pat, e).unwrap();
match bindings.get(Symbol::new("y_")).unwrap() { MatchValue::Single(v) => assert_eq!(v.to_string(), "5"), _ => {}
} Within Add and Mul, matching is associative and commutative : arguments are sorted and matched in a canonical order.

